WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.138 --> 00:00:02.760
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.840
- [Narrator] This boat isn't going

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.360
to an exotic holiday destination.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.940
It's taking us to Obi
Islands to get a rare look

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.970
inside one of Indonesia's
largest nickel plants.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.390
This factory is key in the
global nickel supply chain.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.070
Indonesia is by far the world's

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.600
largest producer of the metal,

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.370
an essential component for batteries

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.130
that power electric
vehicles around the world.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.860
But getting the nickel out
of the ground is dirty work

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.690
and environmentally conscious consumers

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.970
may not be fully aware
of how polluting it is

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.290
to obtain the metal.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.480
- The pickle for the EV makers

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.780
is how do we get this nickel that we need

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.370
without hurting our reputation

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.500
and also without hurting the environment?

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.670
- [Narrator] We take an inside look

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.230
at nickel's growing importance

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.513
and the environmental
toll it leaves behind.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.680
Nickel is used in batteries

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.840
because it increases in EV's range.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.760
Batteries with lots of
nickel can run farther

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.010
than batteries that
don't use the material.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.800
- Nickel is the cheapest and
the highest energy density

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.600
and that's why increasing nickel

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.450
is a goal of ours and really
everybody's in the energy,

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.640
in the battery industry.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.470
- [Narrator] For years,
nickel had been sourced

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.480
from countries such as Canada and Russia,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.550
where the metal is
buried deep underground,

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.190
which makes it expensive to extract.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.290
That's why car makers
are turning to Indonesia

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.330
where nickel is found
close to the surface.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.650
- And what that means is that

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.900
it's actually relatively cheap to get to.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.580
You don't have to do some big

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.280
sophisticated tunnel system
underneath the ground.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.500
The problem is that a lot of the nickel

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.730
overlaps with forests,

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.780
so when you're clearing the land

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.960
what you're doing is you're
clearing rain forest.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.460
- [Narrator] Increasingly,
plants are using

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.800
a process called, high
pressure acid leaching

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.990
to extract a nickel
from the ore found here.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.720
- [Jon] What that involves
is subjecting the nickel

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.530
to extremely high temperatures
and high pressures

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.840
and it ultimately turns
it into a substance

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.420
that can be used in batteries.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.580
- [Narrator] This method is
about twice as carbon intensive

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.280
as other processes used
in Russia or Canada

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.500
leaving behind large amounts of waste.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.750
- It's another challenge for car makers

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.540
when they're contemplating
sorting nickel from Indonesia

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.640
is that these islands in Eastern Indonesia

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:09.180
are very pristine, they're
surrounded by coral reefs.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.460
If there's leakage from
the nickel into the reefs

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.290
that can be quite bad.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.390
- [Narrator] Nickel mining often
takes place in remote parts

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.580
of the country that are
difficult to access.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.130
This plant on Obi Island
is a full day's journey

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.250
from the capital Jakarta and
can only be reached by boat.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.440
- There are concerns that
there isn't that much oversight

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.620
over this process and that the
local government departments,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.470
although they may intend to enforce

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.750
Indonesian environmental
law quite tightly,

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.900
they may really struggle to do that.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.370
- [Narrator] A lot of
the forest being cleared

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.040
is being done legally
according to Indonesian law.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.620
- So it becomes a bit tricky for companies

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.110
because it's ultimately Indonesia,

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.790
and Indonesia is saying this is okay,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.680
but if it's okay for Indonesia government

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.720
should that necessarily
mean it's okay for Tesla?

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.720
These are questions that
I think Tesla is asking.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.730
- [Narrator] Tesla and other
automakers have in recent years

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.980
dispatched teams to
Indonesia to understand

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.473
the full scope of the
environmental concerns.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.130
Despite its toll on the environment,

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.010
nickel mining has seen
explosive growth in the country.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.920
- Indonesia's government sees nickel

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.530
as a way for it to move
up the value chains.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.870
- [Narrator] In 2017,
Indonesia was a minor player

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.570
in the EV battery nickel supply chain

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:21.510
but today about half of the
world's nickel is mined here.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.220
- They've restricted the export of nickel

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.290
so it has to be processed in country,

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.610
so once the nickel's processed

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.680
they're hoping that batteries
will be built in Indonesia,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.150
maybe exported from Indonesia,

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.010
the cars will be built in Indonesia.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.920
That's the Indonesian
government's game plan.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.290
- [Narrator] Some analysts
forecast that by 2027,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.510
about 80% of the global nickel supply

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.300
used in EV batteries
will come from Indonesia.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.730
To mitigate the damage
done by clearing forests

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.150
companies have pledged to
replant trees over mined areas,

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:49.560
and the government has enforced laws

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.180
that punish illegal mining,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.850
but environmentalists say
corporate planting programs

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.850
won't restore the area's
unique flora and fauna.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.310
- It's very difficult and
requires a lot of expertise

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.160
and a lot of money to really
restore an environment,

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.770
especially in a delicate
ecosystem like this.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.240
So there are a lot of questions about

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.603
what these islands are gonna
look like 10 years from now.

